THOUGHT: Marking `gameLoop` as `@Nullable` fixed the FIELD_NO_INIT error but introduced new NullAway errors where `gameLoop` is dereferenced. To keep behavior and satisfy NullAway, I should (1) make `loop()` return a non-null `IGameLoop` by throwing if `gameLoop` is null, and (2) replace direct dereferences in `setUncaughtExceptionHandler`, `start`, and `terminate` with calls to `loop()`. This preserves the existing contract that callers must initialize the game before use and avoids nullable dereferences.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '347,349c\  public static IGameLoop loop() {
    if (gameLoop == null) {
      throw new IllegalStateException("The game loop is not initialized. Call Game.init(...) before accessing the game loop.");
    }

    return gameLoop;
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/Game.java && sed -i '514s/gameLoop/loop()/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/Game.java && sed -i '541s/gameLoop/loop()/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/Game.java && sed -i '623s/gameLoop/loop()/' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/Game.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "Game.java" new_build_output.log || echo "DONE_CHECK_LOG_SEPARATELY"
```

